Meaning: Preventive - Planned maintenance done before a fault occurs;
   Corrective - Maintenance done after a fault or breakdown occurs
   Purpose: Preventive - To prevent breakdown and extend equipment life;
   Corrective - To repair the fault and restore the equipment to working condition
   Timing: Preventive - Scheduled / regular (daily, weekly, monthly); Corrective -
   Unscheduled, when a failure happens
   Examples: Preventive - Cleaning, oiling, adjusting, routine replacement of parts;
   Corrective - Fixing a broken part, replacing a part after breakdown

   Cost / downtime: Preventive - Lower cost, less downtime; Corrective - Higher cost,
   more downtime

